      "id": 1,
      "text": "Climax got its quirky name from the Climax chewing tobacco brand, a nod to 19th‑century marketing rather than a dramatic landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climax%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1896, Climax sprang up as a railroad town along the St. Paul, Minneapolis & Manitoba line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/climax_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers were largely Norwegian and other Scandinavian immigrants drawn by fertile Red River Valley soils.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/climax_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, Climax’s economy centers on grain and sugar beet farming, with small‑scale services, education, and health care supporting the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/climax_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Sand Hill River runs through Climax, joining the Red River of the North just two miles west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climax%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
